#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
YARA tests for detections/yara/php2shell_hunt.yar

Sample contents are stored base64-encoded and written to a temporary directory only at run time, so no web-shell
text sits in the repository (antivirus engines otherwise block this file on checkout).
Session samples marked "real PHP 8.3.6" were produced by a PHP 8.3.6 server receiving benign test requests; the
others are hand-built in the same serialized format. Expected = rule name, None (must not match) or "GAP"
(documented false negative: reported, not counted as a failure).

Run:  pip install yara-python && python3 tests/test_yara.py
"""
